AudD  ·  profile default
                 │ Help › Keys
 1 Recognize     │  Getting started  Guide  Commands >Keys< Exit codes  Links 
 2 Now playing   │ Moving around
 3 Streams       │   Menu on the left, page on the right. Arrows move, Enter goes in, Esc comes back.
 4 Recognitions  │   The menu is the sidebar; Help, Streams, Recognitions, and Account have a tab bar above their page.
 5 Account       │   On a choice ‹ like this ›, ←/→ change it and ← on its first option goes back. When a text field is
 6 Settings      │   selected, you are typing in it: letters, digits, and symbols go in, ←/→ move the cursor (← at its
*7 Help          >   start goes back), ctrl+u clears it, and esc stops typing. Recognize opens typing in Input; other
                 │   pages open with no text field selected, so 1-7 jump to a section. A saved value, such as the
                 │   callback URL, is changed only after enter or e, and esc puts the old value back. Enter in a form's
                 │   last text field runs it (in Add a stream, enter in ID adds it; the box below is optional). What a
                 │   page can do is on its buttons: tab (or ↓ from the end of the page) reaches them, ←/→ move between
                 │   them, enter presses one. A letter on a button, such as (o), presses it from anywhere on the page. A
                 │   key works only where it is listed; any other key says it does nothing. Settings of audd save right
                 │   away (u undoes the last change). Spending more than one request, removing, signing out, or
                 │   replacing the token asks in a dialog: enter presses the focused button (the action after a plan,
                 │   Cancel otherwise), y confirms, n or esc cancels; in a dialog y confirms instead of copying the
                 │   command.
                 │ 
                 │   ↑/↓            move in the menu, a list, or a form
                 │   → or enter     go in: open the section, the page, the selected item
                 │   ← or esc       come back one level (in typed text ← moves the cursor)
                 │   ←/→            on a tab bar: switch tabs; on a choice: change it
                 │   ↑              from the top of a page: back to its tab bar
                 │   [ ]            previous or next tab, from anywhere in the section outside text fields
                 │ 
                 │ Everywhere
                 │   1-7            jump to a section (not while typing in a text field)
                 │   ctrl+k or :    run any command; ctrl+k again closes it
                 │   y              copy the command shown at the bottom (in a dialog: confirm)
                 │   ?              keys for this screen
                 │   F1             help
                 │   q              quit; not while typing, and it asks while a command runs
                 │   ctrl+c         quit, also while typing (it asks while a command runs)
 [ Commands ]    │   ctrl+u         clear the field being typed in
 [ Keys ] q quit │ ↓ 69 more lines below

